{{Quote|Two squads of stormtroopers should be more than enough to handle one alien.|[[Captain]] [[Voss Parck]], underestimating the [[Chiss]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]]|<ref name="Thrawn 1">[[Thrawn 1|''Thrawn'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:Squad_Tactics_SWDConv.png|thumb|right|250px|A clone cadet squad training on Kamino.]]
A '''squad''' was generally a part of a larger military formation and consisted of a unit of [[soldier]]s or operators,<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> who themselves could be broken down into [[fire team]]s.<ref name="Witness">{{StoryCite|story=The Witness|book=From a Certain Point of View: The Empire Strikes Back}}</ref>

In the [[Grand Army of the Republic]], a squad was made up of nine [[clone trooper]]s commanded by a [[Clone Sergeant|clone sergeant]]. Each [[platoon]] consisted of four squads.<ref name="CL" /> In the [[Stormtrooper Corps]], a squad was made up of ten [[stormtrooper]]s. Each platoon was composed of five squads.<ref name="SuperGraphic">''[[Star Wars Super Graphic: A Visual Guide to a Galaxy Far, Far Away]]''</ref> Likewise, the [[First Order]]'s [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] squads were made up of ten [[trooper]]s,<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> as were squads of [[Sith trooper]]s in the [[Sith Eternal military]].<ref name="SWCEUAE">''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> Each First Order squad contained nine ordinary stormtrooper slots and one specialist slot. This was the standard operational unit for First Order stormtroopers, and squadmates had often trained with each other in large classes known as batches.<ref name="CVD" /> In the [[Sith Eternal army]], squads were broken down into fire team-level units known as [[Triad (unit)|triads]].<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

